    51 │ }
  
  i The original error is declared here.
  
    44 │ try {
    45 │     doSomething();
  > 46 │ } catch (error) {
       │          ^^^^^
    47 │     if (whatever) {
    48 │         const error = anotherError; // This declaration is the problem.
  
  i The `cause` refers to a different value than the caught error, so the original error is still lost.
  
  i Rename the variable that shadows the caught error, or pass the caught error as the `cause`.
  

